{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "sit_014",
  "kind": "process",
  "title": "Handle a security-vulnerability report",
  "summary": "Someone who reports a vulnerability in good faith is doing you a favor. Don't make them wait. Reply fast and open a private channel; ignored researchers go public. Reproduce the bug as they described it. Judge severity by exploitability, not embarrassment. Fix it on the timeline the severity justifies. Agree a disclosure date with the reporter (90-day coordinated disclosure is industry practice, not law) and publish the advisory with credit. Follow CISA's coordinated-vulnerability-disclosure guidance. A security.txt file sends the next report to you instead of your CEO's inbox. If the hole was exploited and data was reached, switch to 'Respond to a data breach': different situation, statutory deadlines.",
